<header><p class="st-kicker">tribal confederation · Balkans and Hungary</p><h1 class="st-title">Seven Slavic Tribes</h1><p class="st-meta">600 CE – 681 CE (approx.)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Union of Slavic tribes in Moesia that joined Asparuh's Bulgars in 681, forming one of the two founding peoples of Bulgaria.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>After the collapse of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/danube">Danube</a> frontier in the early 7th century, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slavs">Slavs</a> settled densely in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moesia">Moesia</a> between the Danube and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/balkan-mountains">Balkan Mountains</a>. Byzantine chroniclers, chiefly <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theophanes-the-confessor">Theophanes</a>, say seven tribes there formed a union, though their names are not recorded.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Little is known beyond a few lines in Byzantine chronicles. The union was a loose alliance of farming tribes under their own chiefs, probably formed against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/avars">Avar</a> and Byzantine pressure. When <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asparuh-of-bulgaria">Asparuh's</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bulgars">Bulgars</a> crossed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/danube">Danube</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slavs">Slavs</a> were placed to guard the western frontier against the Avars, while the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/severians-balkan">Severi</a> held the eastern passes.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 681 <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/byzantium">Byzantium</a> recognised the new <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bulgars">Bulgar</a> state, and the union was absorbed into the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/first-bulgarian-empire">First Bulgarian Empire</a>. Over the next two centuries <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slavs">Slavs</a> and Bulgars merged, and the Slavic language prevailed.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/seven-slavic-tribes.jpg" alt="Seven Slavic Tribes" width="320" height="465"><figcaption>Image: Kandi · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Balkans_about_680_A.D.,_foundation_of_the_First_Bulgarian_Empire.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>600 CE – 681 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>tribal confederation</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Slavic paganism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Old Slavic</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/bulgaria">Bulgaria</a>, <a href="/countries/romania">Romania</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Union of the Seven Slavic Tribes, Seven Slavic clans</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=640&amp;focus=seven-slavic-tribes" aria-label="Seven Slavic Tribes on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5290 659 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Seven Slavic Tribes lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5653 895h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5610 915h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M5610 915h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day Bulgaria. <a href="/atlas?year=640&amp;focus=seven-slavic-tribes">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
